# .trivyignore — unfixable CVEs suppressed from the gating Trivy scan.
#
# All entries below have been reviewed and are unfixable at this time.
# Each is documented in SECURITY.md with the rationale and a tracking reference.
#
# Pruned 2026-11-15: every AL2023 OS-package, python3-pip RPM, and
# supercronic Go stdlib entry was removed after `dnf upgrade
# --releasever=latest` and the digest-pinned aws-backup-base 1.2.2 cleared
# them (verified with an unsuppressed `trivy image --ignore-unfixed
# --severity HIGH,CRITICAL` scan). Only findings with no installable fix
# remain.
#
# ── urllib3 (pip 2.6.3): fix requires 2.7.0 (Python >= 3.10) ───────────────
# urllib3 2.7.0 declares requires_python ">=3.10"; the base image ships
# Python 3.9, and awscli-2 2.38.0 also pins urllib3 <= 2.6.3. The dnf
# python3-urllib3 RPM (1.25.10) has no AL2023 RPM fix either.
CVE-2026-44431
CVE-2026-44432

# ── urllib3 (pip 2.6.3): fix requires 2.8.0 (Python >= 3.10) ───────────────
# Added 2026-11-15. CVE-2026-97687 (HTTPS-proxy TLS configuration override)
# and CVE-2026-97689 (chunk-parser memory DoS) are fixed only in urllib3
# 2.8.0, whose PyPI metadata declares requires_python ">=3.10" (verified
# 2026-11-15). The base image ships Python 3.9, so no installable fix
# exists. Same root cause as CVE-2026-44431. See SECURITY.md.
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689
